IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sda-common`
IMPORT `fhog-terms`
IMPORT `fhog-grant`

-- First Home and Housing Construction Grants Act 2000 (SA) and Regulations 2015 -- cases for the grant core
-- (fhog-terms.l4, fhog-grant.l4).
--
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited texts (the Act as at 2025-02-13, a later version exists;
-- the Regulations as at 2021-03-11), never copied from this encoding's output. Dates were counted on a calendar.
-- Regulative rules are asserted with EVALTRACE where the trace ends FULFILLED, and #TRACEd with an "-- expect:" line
-- where it ends in a breach or a pending obligation. Clock: days. "The relevant day" (s 11(4)) is an INPUT: 13 February
-- 2025, the commencement of s 4 of the Statutes Amendment (Budget Measures) Act 2025 as the deposited legislative
-- history records it (NOTES.md, finding 3).
--
-- Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website (CC BY 4.0). Not the official text. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the applicant for a first home owner grant`

`the relevant day in the grant cases` MEANS YMD 2025 2 13

§§ `ss 3-6 -- the shared terms`

#ASSERT `the building is a home (s 4)` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the building is a home (s 4)` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the building is a home (s 4)` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the home is a new home (s 3)` FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`the home is a new home (s 3)` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the home is a new home (s 3)` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`the home is a new home (s 3)` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the land is residential property (s 3)` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the land is residential property (s 3)` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the land is residential property (s 3)` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the interest is a relevant interest (s 5)` `an estate in fee simple` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`the interest is a relevant interest (s 5)` `an estate in fee simple` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the interest is a relevant interest (s 5)` `an estate in fee simple` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the interest is a relevant interest (s 5)` `an estate in fee simple` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the interest is a relevant interest (s 5)` `an estate in fee simple` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `the interest is a relevant interest (s 5)` `a perpetual lease granted by the Commonwealth or the State` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`the interest is a relevant interest (s 5)` `some other interest` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the person is an owner of a home (s 5(1))` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is an owner of a home (s 5(1))` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the person is the applicant's spouse (s 6(1), (2))` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is the applicant's spouse (s 6(1), (2))` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the person is the applicant's spouse (s 6(1), (2))` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `the person is the applicant's domestic partner (s 6(1a))` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is the applicant's domestic partner (s 6(1a))` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is the applicant's domestic partner (s 6(1a))` TRUE TRUE FALSE)

§§ `An application, with the facts most cases share`

-- Individual applicants, of age, at least one a citizen, no earlier grant or property, all owners applying, applying
-- within the period. The parameters are the facts that vary between cases.
GIVEN `kind`                  IS A `Kind of transaction`
      `new`                   IS A BOOLEAN
      `commenced`             IS A DATE
      `completed`             IS A BOOLEAN
      `completion`            IS A DATE
      `consideration`         IS A NUMBER
      `held property before`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `lived in it 6 months`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `applied`               IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Grant application`
`an application` MEANS
    `Grant application` WITH
        `the kind of transaction`                                                       IS `kind`
        `the home is a new home`                                                        IS `new`
        `the commencement date`                                                         IS `commenced`
        `the transaction has been completed`                                            IS `completed`
        `the date of completion`                                                        IS `completion`
        `the consideration`                                                             IS `consideration`
        `the Commissioner considers the consideration may be less than the market value` IS FALSE
        `the market value as determined by the Commissioner`                            IS `consideration`
        `the Commissioner considers the building consideration may be less than the actual costs to build the home` IS FALSE
        `the actual costs to build the home as determined by the Commissioner`          IS 0
        `the Commissioner is of the opinion it is a scheme to circumvent the Act`        IS FALSE
        `every applicant is a natural person`                                           IS TRUE
        `every applicant is at least 18, or exempted by the Commissioner`                IS TRUE
        `at least one applicant is an Australian citizen or permanent resident`         IS TRUE
        `an applicant or spouse was a party to an earlier application on which a grant was paid` IS FALSE
        `that grant was repaid for a residence or condition failure, with any s 39(3) penalty paid` IS FALSE
        `an applicant or spouse could have successfully applied for a grant on an earlier transaction` IS FALSE
        `an applicant or spouse held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000` IS FALSE
        `an applicant or spouse held a relevant interest in residential property before the commencement date` IS `held property before`
        `an applicant or spouse occupied that property as a residence for 6 continuous months` IS `lived in it 6 months`
        `the relevant day`                                                              IS `the relevant day in the grant cases`
        `every interested person is an applicant`                                       IS TRUE
        `the date of the application`                                                   IS `applied`
        `the Commissioner allows the application outside the application period`        IS FALSE

-- A new home bought under a contract of 1 May 2026 for $550 000, completed on 1 August 2026, applied for on
-- 1 September 2026.
`the 2026 new home application` MEANS
    `an application` `a contract for the purchase of a home in the State` TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 8 1) 550000 FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 9 1)

#ASSERT `the transaction is an eligible transaction (s 13)` `the 2026 new home application`
#ASSERT `it is a new home transaction (s 3)` `the 2026 new home application`
#ASSERT `criteria 1 to 4 are met` `the 2026 new home application`
#ASSERT `the market value cap (s 7(1a))` `the 2026 new home application` EQUALS `no cap`
#ASSERT `the first home owner grant is payable (s 7)` `the 2026 new home application` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the first home owner grant is payable (s 7)` `the 2026 new home application` FALSE)
#ASSERT `the amount of the first home owner grant (s 18)` `the 2026 new home application` EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 15000

-- s 18(1)(a): the lesser of the consideration and $15 000 -- a building contract for $9 500 gets $9 500.
#ASSERT `the amount of the first home owner grant (s 18)` (`an application` `a comprehensive home building contract for a home in the State` TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) TRUE (YMD 2027 3 1) 9500 FALSE FALSE (YMD 2027 4 1)) EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 9500
-- An owner builder of a new home: a new home transaction, $15 000.
#ASSERT `the amount of the first home owner grant (s 18)` (`an application` `the building of a home in the State by an owner builder` TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) TRUE (YMD 2027 5 1) 300000 FALSE FALSE (YMD 2027 6 1)) EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 15000
-- s 18(4a): an established home bought in 2026 gets nothing.
#ASSERT `the amount of the first home owner grant (s 18)` (`an application` `a contract for the purchase of a home in the State` FALSE (YMD 2026 5 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 8 1) 550000 FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 9 1)) EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 0
#ASSERT NOT (`it is a new home transaction (s 3)` (`an application` `a contract for the purchase of a home in the State` FALSE (YMD 2026 5 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 8 1) 550000 FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 9 1)))
-- 15 October 2012 is the first day of the $15 000; before it, `not covered`. Established homes before 1 July 2014,
-- `not covered`.
#ASSERT `the amount of the first home owner grant (s 18)` (`an application` `a contract for the purchase of a home in the State` TRUE (YMD 2012 10 15) TRUE (YMD 2013 1 15) 400000 FALSE FALSE (YMD 2013 2 1)) EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 15000
#ASSERT `the amount of the first home owner grant (s 18)` (`an application` `a contract for the purchase of a home in the State` TRUE (YMD 2012 10 14) TRUE (YMD 2013 1 15) 400000 FALSE FALSE (YMD 2013 2 1)) EQUALS `not covered` `the grant amounts before 15 October 2012 involve bonus grants whose formulas are missing (ss 18B, 18BA) and are not encoded`
#ASSERT `the amount of the first home owner grant (s 18)` (`an application` `a contract for the purchase of a home in the State` FALSE (YMD 2014 6 30) TRUE (YMD 2014 9 1) 400000 FALSE FALSE (YMD 2014 9 2)) EQUALS `not covered` `the grant amount for a transaction other than a new home transaction before 1 July 2014 turns on the 2012 statutory date and is not encoded`
#ASSERT `the amount of the first home owner grant (s 18)` (`an application` `a contract for the purchase of a home in the State` FALSE (YMD 2014 7 1) TRUE (YMD 2014 9 1) 400000 FALSE FALSE (YMD 2014 9 2)) EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 0

§§ `s 7(1a) and s 18BB -- the market value cap`

-- 1 January 2024: a cap of $650 000. $640 000 is within it; $660 000 is not.
#ASSERT `the market value cap (s 7(1a))` (`an application` `a contract for the purchase of a home in the State` TRUE (YMD 2024 1 1) TRUE (YMD 2024 3 1) 640000 FALSE FALSE (YMD 2024 3 2)) EQUALS `a cap of` 650000
#ASSERT `the first home owner grant is payable (s 7)` (`an application` `a contract for the purchase of a home in the State` TRUE (YMD 2024 1 1) TRUE (YMD 2024 3 1) 640000 FALSE FALSE (YMD 2024 3 2)) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the first home owner grant is payable (s 7)` (`an application` `a contract for the purchase of a home in the State` TRUE (YMD 2024 1 1) TRUE (YMD 2024 3 1) 660000 FALSE FALSE (YMD 2024 3 2)) TRUE)
-- 1 January 2023: a cap of $575 000.
#ASSERT `the market value cap (s 7(1a))` (`an application` `a contract for the purchase of a home in the State` TRUE (YMD 2023 1 1) TRUE (YMD 2023 3 1) 600000 FALSE FALSE (YMD 2023 3 2)) EQUALS `a cap of` 575000
#ASSERT NOT (`the market value is within the cap (s 7(1a))` (`an application` `a contract for the purchase of a home in the State` TRUE (YMD 2023 1 1) TRUE (YMD 2023 3 1) 600000 FALSE FALSE (YMD 2023 3 2)))
-- 15 June 2023 starts the $650 000 cap; 6 June 2024 ends it.
#ASSERT `the market value cap (s 7(1a))` (`an application` `a contract for the purchase of a home in the State` TRUE (YMD 2023 6 15) TRUE (YMD 2023 9 1) 600000 FALSE FALSE (YMD 2023 9 2)) EQUALS `a cap of` 650000
#ASSERT `the market value cap (s 7(1a))` (`an application` `a contract for the purchase of a home in the State` TRUE (YMD 2024 6 6) TRUE (YMD 2024 9 1) 900000 FALSE FALSE (YMD 2024 9 2)) EQUALS `no cap`
-- Before 17 September 2010 there was no cap under s 7(1a).
#ASSERT `the market value cap (s 7(1a))` (`an application` `a contract for the purchase of a home in the State` TRUE (YMD 2010 9 16) TRUE (YMD 2010 12 1) 600000 FALSE FALSE (YMD 2010 12 2)) EQUALS `no cap`

-- s 18BB(1)(b): for a comprehensive home building contract the market value is the SUM of the building price (or the
-- actual costs as the Commissioner determines them, if the Commissioner considers the price may be less) and the
-- Commissioner's market value of the property on which the home is to be built, when the contract is made. A building
-- contract for a new home commencing on 1 January 2024 (cap $650 000), completed 1 September 2024, applied for on
-- 15 September 2024. Parameters: the building price, whether the Commissioner considers it may be less than the actual
-- costs, those costs, and the land's market value.
GIVEN `price`        IS A NUMBER
      `too low`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `actual costs` IS A NUMBER
      `land value`   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Grant application`
`a building contract application` MEANS
    `Grant application` WITH
        `the kind of transaction`                                                       IS `a comprehensive home building contract for a home in the State`
        `the home is a new home`                                                        IS TRUE
        `the commencement date`                                                         IS YMD 2024 1 1
        `the transaction has been completed`                                            IS TRUE
        `the date of completion`                                                        IS YMD 2024 9 1
        `the consideration`                                                             IS `price`
        `the Commissioner considers the consideration may be less than the market value` IS FALSE
        `the market value as determined by the Commissioner`                            IS `land value`
        `the Commissioner considers the building consideration may be less than the actual costs to build the home` IS `too low`
        `the actual costs to build the home as determined by the Commissioner`          IS `actual costs`
        `the Commissioner is of the opinion it is a scheme to circumvent the Act`        IS FALSE
        `every applicant is a natural person`                                           IS TRUE
        `every applicant is at least 18, or exempted by the Commissioner`                IS TRUE
        `at least one applicant is an Australian citizen or permanent resident`         IS TRUE
        `an applicant or spouse was a party to an earlier application on which a grant was paid` IS FALSE
        `that grant was repaid for a residence or condition failure, with any s 39(3) penalty paid` IS FALSE
        `an applicant or spouse could have successfully applied for a grant on an earlier transaction` IS FALSE
        `an applicant or spouse held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000` IS FALSE
        `an applicant or spouse held a relevant interest in residential property before the commencement date` IS FALSE
        `an applicant or spouse occupied that property as a residence for 6 continuous months` IS FALSE
        `the relevant day`                                                              IS `the relevant day in the grant cases`
        `every interested person is an applicant`                                       IS TRUE
        `the date of the application`                                                   IS YMD 2024 9 15
        `the Commissioner allows the application outside the application period`        IS FALSE

-- $400 000 to build on land worth $300 000: $700 000, over the $650 000 cap, so no grant.
#ASSERT `the market value of the home (s 18BB)` (`a building contract application` 400000 FALSE 0 300000) EQUALS 700000
#ASSERT NOT (`the market value is within the cap (s 7(1a))` (`a building contract application` 400000 FALSE 0 300000))
#ASSERT NOT (`the first home owner grant is payable (s 7)` (`a building contract application` 400000 FALSE 0 300000) TRUE)
-- $300 000 to build on the same land: $600 000, within the cap; the grant is the lesser of $300 000 and $15 000.
#ASSERT `the market value of the home (s 18BB)` (`a building contract application` 300000 FALSE 0 300000) EQUALS 600000
#ASSERT `the first home owner grant is payable (s 7)` (`a building contract application` 300000 FALSE 0 300000) TRUE
-- The Commissioner considers $300 000 too low and puts the actual costs at $380 000: $680 000, over the cap.
#ASSERT `the market value of the home (s 18BB)` (`a building contract application` 300000 TRUE 380000 300000) EQUALS 680000
#ASSERT NOT (`the market value is within the cap (s 7(1a))` (`a building contract application` 300000 TRUE 380000 300000))
-- The cap compares "exceeds": $350 000 on $300 000 of land is exactly $650 000, within it.
#ASSERT `the market value is within the cap (s 7(1a))` (`a building contract application` 350000 FALSE 0 300000)
-- An owner builder: the Commissioner's market value of land and home at completion alone (s 18BB(1)(c)).
#ASSERT `the market value of the home (s 18BB)` (`an application` `the building of a home in the State by an owner builder` TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) TRUE (YMD 2027 5 1) 300000 FALSE FALSE (YMD 2027 6 1)) EQUALS 300000

§§ `ss 7 and 18 -- the grant payable on the application`

#ASSERT `the first home owner grant payable on the application (ss 7, 18)` `the 2026 new home application` TRUE EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 15000
-- The residence requirement not met and not paid in anticipation: nothing yet.
#ASSERT `the first home owner grant payable on the application (ss 7, 18)` `the 2026 new home application` FALSE EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 0
#ASSERT `the first home owner grant payable on the application (ss 7, 18)` (`a building contract application` 400000 FALSE 0 300000) TRUE EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 0
#ASSERT `the first home owner grant payable on the application (ss 7, 18)` (`a building contract application` 300000 FALSE 0 300000) TRUE EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 15000

§§ `ss 8-11 -- the criteria`

-- s 11(3): from the relevant day, a relevant interest held before bars, even if never lived in.
#ASSERT NOT (`criterion 4 is met (s 11)` (`an application` `a contract for the purchase of a home in the State` TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 8 1) 550000 TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 9 1)))
-- Before the relevant day (1 December 2024), it bars only if lived in for 6 continuous months.
#ASSERT `criterion 4 is met (s 11)` (`an application` `a contract for the purchase of a home in the State` TRUE (YMD 2024 12 1) TRUE (YMD 2025 3 1) 550000 TRUE FALSE (YMD 2025 3 2))
#ASSERT NOT (`criterion 4 is met (s 11)` (`an application` `a contract for the purchase of a home in the State` TRUE (YMD 2024 12 1) TRUE (YMD 2025 3 1) 550000 TRUE TRUE (YMD 2025 3 2)))

-- The other criteria, one at a time, on the 2026 application.
GIVEN `natural`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `of age`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `citizen`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `earlier paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `repaid`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `could have`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `before 2000` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all join`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `scheme`      IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Grant application`
`the 2026 application, but` MEANS
    `Grant application` WITH
        `the kind of transaction`                                                       IS `a contract for the purchase of a home in the State`
        `the home is a new home`                                                        IS TRUE
        `the commencement date`                                                         IS YMD 2026 5 1
        `the transaction has been completed`                                            IS TRUE
        `the date of completion`                                                        IS YMD 2026 8 1
        `the consideration`                                                             IS 550000
        `the Commissioner considers the consideration may be less than the market value` IS FALSE
        `the market value as determined by the Commissioner`                            IS 550000
        `the Commissioner considers the building consideration may be less than the actual costs to build the home` IS FALSE
        `the actual costs to build the home as determined by the Commissioner`          IS 0
        `the Commissioner is of the opinion it is a scheme to circumvent the Act`        IS `scheme`
        `every applicant is a natural person`                                           IS `natural`
        `every applicant is at least 18, or exempted by the Commissioner`                IS `of age`
        `at least one applicant is an Australian citizen or permanent resident`         IS `citizen`
        `an applicant or spouse was a party to an earlier application on which a grant was paid` IS `earlier paid`
        `that grant was repaid for a residence or condition failure, with any s 39(3) penalty paid` IS `repaid`
        `an applicant or spouse could have successfully applied for a grant on an earlier transaction` IS `could have`
        `an applicant or spouse held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000` IS `before 2000`
        `an applicant or spouse held a relevant interest in residential property before the commencement date` IS FALSE
        `an applicant or spouse occupied that property as a residence for 6 continuous months` IS FALSE
        `the relevant day`                                                              IS `the relevant day in the grant cases`
        `every interested person is an applicant`                                       IS `all join`
        `the date of the application`                                                   IS YMD 2026 9 1
        `the Commissioner allows the application outside the application period`        IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the first home owner grant is payable (s 7)` (`the 2026 application, but` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`criteria 1 to 4 are met` (`the 2026 application, but` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`criteria 1 to 4 are met` (`the 2026 application, but` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`criteria 1 to 4 are met` (`the 2026 application, but` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`criteria 1 to 4 are met` (`the 2026 application, but` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE))
-- s 10(2): an earlier grant repaid for failing the residence requirement, with any penalty paid, does not bar.
#ASSERT `criteria 1 to 4 are met` (`the 2026 application, but` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`criteria 1 to 4 are met` (`the 2026 application, but` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`criteria 1 to 4 are met` (`the 2026 application, but` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the first home owner grant is payable (s 7)` (`the 2026 application, but` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the transaction is an eligible transaction (s 13)` (`the 2026 application, but` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE))

§§ `s 14(5) -- the application period`

-- Completed 1 August 2026: the period ends on 1 August 2027.
#ASSERT `the last day of the application period (s 14(5))` `the 2026 new home application` EQUALS YMD 2027 8 1
#ASSERT `the application is made within the application period (s 14(5), (6))` (`an application` `a contract for the purchase of a home in the State` TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 8 1) 550000 FALSE FALSE (YMD 2027 8 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`the application is made within the application period (s 14(5), (6))` (`an application` `a contract for the purchase of a home in the State` TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 8 1) 550000 FALSE FALSE (YMD 2027 8 2)))
-- Before the commencement date: outside the period.
#ASSERT NOT (`the application is made within the application period (s 14(5), (6))` (`an application` `a contract for the purchase of a home in the State` TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 8 1) 550000 FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 4 30)))
-- Not yet completed: an application after the commencement date is within the period.
#ASSERT `the application is made within the application period (s 14(5), (6))` (`an application` `a contract for the purchase of a home in the State` TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 5 1) 550000 FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 6 1))
-- But the grant is not payable until completion (s 7(1)(b)(ii)).
#ASSERT NOT (`the first home owner grant is payable (s 7)` (`an application` `a contract for the purchase of a home in the State` TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 5 1) 550000 FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 6 1)) TRUE)
-- The rule. 1 May 2026 to 1 August 2027 is 457 days.
#ASSERT `the days from` (YMD 2026 5 1) `to` (YMD 2027 8 1) EQUALS 457
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 14(5) -- apply between the commencement date and 12 months after completion` 457) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` `apply to the Commissioner for the grant` 123), (EVENT `the Commissioner of State Taxation` `give the applicant notice of the decision on the application` 160)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 14(5) -- apply between the commencement date and 12 months after completion` 457) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 458), (EVENT `the applicant` `apply to the Commissioner for the grant` 470)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: the Commissioner's notice of the decision, pending (applied on day 123)
#TRACE `s 14(5) -- apply between the commencement date and 12 months after completion` 457 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the applicant` DOES `apply to the Commissioner for the grant` AT 123

§§ `s 18C`

#ASSERT `the total grants payable after s 18C` 20000 15000 EQUALS 15000
#ASSERT `the total grants payable after s 18C` 15000 550000 EQUALS 15000

§§ `s 12 and s 20 -- the residence requirement`

-- Completed on 1 August 2026: begin by 1 August 2027; a longer approved period of 18 months: 1 February 2028.
#ASSERT `the last day to begin living in the home (s 12)` (YMD 2026 8 1) 0 EQUALS YMD 2027 8 1
#ASSERT `the last day to begin living in the home (s 12)` (YMD 2026 8 1) 18 EQUALS YMD 2028 2 1
-- Moved in on 1 September 2026: six months ends 1 March 2027; a shorter approved period of 4 months: 1 January 2027.
#ASSERT `the day the residence period ends (s 12)` (YMD 2026 9 1) 0 EQUALS YMD 2027 3 1
#ASSERT `the day the residence period ends (s 12)` (YMD 2026 9 1) 4 EQUALS YMD 2027 1 1
-- s 20(3): completion 1 August 2026, so the residence period must begin by 1 August 2027 and the period allowed ends
-- 1 February 2028. It becomes apparent on 10 March 2027 that the buyers will not move in: notify and repay by
-- 24 March 2027. If it never becomes apparent earlier, 14 days after 1 February 2028: 15 February 2028.
#ASSERT `the end of the period allowed for compliance (s 20(3)(a))` (YMD 2026 8 1) 0 0 EQUALS YMD 2028 2 1
#ASSERT `the last day to notify and repay (s 20(2), (3))` (YMD 2028 2 1) (YMD 2027 3 10) EQUALS YMD 2027 3 24
#ASSERT `the last day to notify and repay (s 20(2), (3))` (YMD 2028 2 1) (YMD 2028 6 1) EQUALS YMD 2028 2 15
#ASSERT `the maximum fine for not notifying and repaying (s 20(4))` EQUALS 5000
-- The rule. Clock: days from completion on 1 August 2026: 365 days to begin; 181 days of residence.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 12 -- live in the home for 6 months, starting within 12 months after completion` `the applicant` 365 181 TRUE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` `begin to live in the home as the applicant's principal place of residence` 31), (WAITUNTIL 250)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 12 -- live in the home for 6 months, starting within 12 months after completion` `a complying applicant, the others exempted by the Commissioner` 365 181 FALSE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `a complying applicant, the others exempted by the Commissioner` `begin to live in the home as the applicant's principal place of residence` 31), (WAITUNTIL 250)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Paid in anticipation, never moved in: notice and repayment within 14 days of the end of the period.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 12 -- live in the home for 6 months, starting within 12 months after completion` `the applicant` 365 181 TRUE) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 366), (EVENT `the applicant` `give the Commissioner written notice that the residence requirement was not complied with` 370), (EVENT `the applicant` `repay the amount of the grant` 378)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Paid in anticipation, moved out after two months: the same 14 days from moving out.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 12 -- live in the home for 6 months, starting within 12 months after completion` `the applicant` 365 181 TRUE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` `begin to live in the home as the applicant's principal place of residence` 31), (EVENT `the applicant` `stop living in the home as the applicant's principal place of residence` 92), (EVENT `the applicant` `give the Commissioner written notice that the residence requirement was not complied with` 95), (EVENT `the applicant` `repay the amount of the grant` 100)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the applicant, "s 20(2)(b), (4): repay the grant within 14 days ..." (notified on day 370, never repaid)
#TRACE `s 12 -- live in the home for 6 months, starting within 12 months after completion` `the applicant` 365 181 TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 366)
    PARTY `the applicant` DOES `give the Commissioner written notice that the residence requirement was not complied with` AT 370
    (WAITUNTIL 390)
-- expect: BREACH BY the applicant, "s 7(1)(a), s 12: the residence requirement is criterion 5; ..." (not paid in anticipation, never moved in)
#TRACE `s 12 -- live in the home for 6 months, starting within 12 months after completion` `the applicant` 365 181 FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 366)

§§ `s 25 -- objection and review`

-- Notice of the decision dated 1 March 2026: object by 30 April 2026; if a retrospective provision was made on
-- 1 April 2026, by 31 May 2026.
#ASSERT `the last day to object to a grant decision (s 25(3))` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 30
#ASSERT `the last day to object to a grant decision (s 25(3))` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 4 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 5 31
#ASSERT `the last day to object to a grant decision (s 25(3))` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2025 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 30
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 25 -- object to the Treasurer within 60 days, then seek review within 60 days` 60) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` `lodge a written notice of objection with the Treasurer` 30), (EVENT `the Treasurer` `give the objector written notice of the decision on the objection` 90), (EVENT `the applicant` `seek a review by the South Australian Civil and Administrative Tribunal` 140)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 25 -- object to the Treasurer within 60 days, then seek review within 60 days` 60) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` `lodge a written notice of objection with the Treasurer` 30), (EVENT `the Treasurer` `give the objector written notice of the decision on the objection` 90), (WAITUNTIL 151)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 25 -- object to the Treasurer within 60 days, then seek review within 60 days` 60) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 61)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: the Treasurer's written notice of the decision on the objection, pending (objection on day 30)
#TRACE `s 25 -- object to the Treasurer within 60 days, then seek review within 60 days` 60 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the applicant` DOES `lodge a written notice of objection with the Treasurer` AT 30

§§ `ss 39, 40 and reg 6 -- repayment, penalty and recovery`

#ASSERT `repayment of the grant can be required (s 39(1))` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `repayment of the grant can be required (s 39(1))` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`repayment of the grant can be required (s 39(1))` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the most penalty under s 39(2) and (3)` 15000 TRUE TRUE EQUALS 30000
#ASSERT `the most penalty under s 39(2) and (3)` 15000 FALSE TRUE EQUALS 15000
#ASSERT `the most penalty under s 39(2) and (3)` 15000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS 15000
#ASSERT `the most penalty under s 39(2) and (3)` 15000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 39 -- repay the amount the Commissioner's notice requires` 28) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` `repay the amount required by the notice` 20)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the applicant, "s 39(3): the repayment required was not made; ..." (not repaid in 28 days)
#TRACE `s 39 -- repay the amount the Commissioner's notice requires` 28 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 29)
#ASSERT `how the repayment is owed (s 40(2), (4))` 2 EQUALS `jointly and severally by the applicants, as a debt due to the Crown`
#ASSERT `how the repayment is owed (s 40(2), (4))` 1 EQUALS `by the one applicant, as a debt due to the Crown`
#ASSERT `the repayment is a first charge on the applicant's interest in the land (s 40(3))` TRUE
#ASSERT `the interest rate on repayment by instalments, per cent a year (reg 6)` 4.35 EQUALS 12.35
